e, maybe L2.\n\nLet's reassign:\n\n- L1: (2,3),(5,1) slope -2/3.\n\n- L2: (2,4) and (4,1) maybe? Slope = (1-4)/(4-2) = -3/2 = -1.5, allowed. So L2: (2,4),(4,1). Good.\n\n- L3: (2,2) and (4,2) slope = (2-2)/(4-2) = 0, horizontal, not allowed. So cannot pair (2,2) with (4,2). Could pair (2,2) with (3,1) slope = (1-2)/(3-2) = -1, not allowed. Pair (2,2) with (3,2) vertical, not allowed. Pair (2,2) with (3,3) slope = (3-2)/(3-2) = 1, allowed. So L3: (2,2),(3,3). Then we need to cover (4,2) maybe with L4.\n\n- L4: (2,1) and (4,2) slope = (2-1)/(4-2) = 1/2 = 0.5, allowed. L4 also could cover (3,? ) maybe (3,? ) but not needed.\n\nNow we have assigned points:\n\n- L1: (2,3),(5,1)\n- L2: (2,4),(4,1)\n- L3: (2,2),(3,3)\n- L4: (2,1),(4,2)\n\nNow we need to cover remaining points: column 3 points (3,1),(3,2) are not covered. Column 4 point (4,? ) we have (4,1) covered by L2, (4,2) covered by L4. So column 4 done. Column 5 done. Column 2 done (all (2,1)-(2,4) covered). So only (3,1) and (3,2) remain.\n\nWe have used all 4 sunny lines, cannot add more. So we need to adjust assignments to also cover (3,1) and (3,2). Perhaps we can assign (3,1) to L2 (which currently has (2,4),(4,1)). Let's see if (2,4),(3,1),(4,1) are collinear? Points (2,4) and (3,1) slope = (1-4)/(3-2) = -3, allowed. Equation: y - 4 = -3 (x - 2) => y = -3x + 10. At x=4, y = -12 + 10 = -2, not 1. So (4,1) not on that line. So cannot have both (2,4) and (4,1) with (3,1) on same line.\n\nMaybe we can assign (3,1) to L3 (currently (2,2),(3,3)). Let's see if (2,2),(3,3),(3,1) collinear? No, (3,1) not on line y = x (since (2,2) and (3,3) define y = x). So not.\n\nAssign (3,1) to L4 (currently (2,1),(4,2)). Check if (2,1),(3,1),(4,2) collinear? (2,1)-(3,1) horizontal, slope 0, not allowed. So no.\n\nThus we need to modify the assignment to include (3,1) and (3,2) in some lines.\n\nPerhaps we can assign (3,1) to L1 (currently (2,3),(5,1)). Let's see if (2,3),(3,1),(5,1) collinear? Compute slope between (2,3) and (3,1) 